\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Three boundary prescriptions}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{In the site basis of \ref{fdip-00HV}, the [whole-space Wick
variance](fdip-00HX) is
##{c_\epsilon(m_0)=\frac1{(2\pi)^2}
 \int_{[-\pi,\pi]^2}
 \frac{dk}{m_0^2\epsilon^2+4\sin^2(k_1/2)+4\sin^2(k_2/2)}.}
This is the covariance of a site evaluation, including the
#{\epsilon^{-2}} conversion from an operator to its kernel for weighted
counting measure. The Fourier formula is
\citet{(IV.6)-(IV.7), p. 193}{guerra1975euclideanII}.}

\p{The [half-Dirichlet law](fdip-00HX) uses this constant with the
Dirichlet Gaussian covariance #{C_{\epsilon,D}}. Full Dirichlet
ordering would instead use #{c_{\epsilon,D}(x)=(C_{\epsilon,D})_{xx}}
in each Wick polynomial. The two interactions differ by quadratic and
constant terms depending on #{x}; they need not give the same finite
law.}

\p{Restricting the whole-space free covariance to the retained sites
gives a third Gaussian. For a finite exterior approximation, write its
precision in the retained/exterior decomposition as
##{\begin{pmatrix}A&B\\B^*&D\end{pmatrix}.}
Its marginal precision is #{A-BD^{-1}B^*}, by \ref{fdip-000D}
and the [conditional Gaussian kernel](fdip-003A); the killed precision
is #{A}. The outward-exterior limit is the boundary correction of
\citet{(IV.16), (IV.18)-(IV.21), Theorem IV.7,
pp. 195-199}{guerra1975euclideanII}.}
